{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For managing acid reflux of the stomach, focusing on alkaline, low-acid, and high-fiber foods can be very beneficial.\n\nHere are some foods that are generally recommended:\n*   **Fruits:** Bananas are highly alkaline and can help lower symptoms. Melons like watermelon, cantaloupe, and honeydew are low in acid. Apples are also thought to help neutralize stomach acid due to their alkalizing minerals.\n*   **Vegetables:** Green vegetables such as asparagus, Brussels sprouts, kale, spinach, broccoli, leafy greens, cucumbers, and green beans are alkaline, low in fat, and promote good digestion. Root vegetables like carrots and sweet potatoes are also good choices.\n*   **Grains:** Oatmeal, whole-grain bread, brown rice, and cous-cous are excellent sources of fiber, which can help absorb stomach acid and promote a healthy digestive system.\n*   **Lean Proteins:** Skinless chicken, turkey, fish (especially oily fish like salmon), tofu, and egg whites are good low-fat protein options. It's best to broil, grill, or saut\u00e9 them, avoiding deep-frying.\n*   **Other beneficial foods:** Ginger is known for its anti-inflammatory properties. Skim or fat-free yogurt, unsweetened coconut water, and nuts like walnuts and almonds (which are alkaline and contain fiber) can also be helpful. Foods with high water content, such as celery and lettuce, are also beneficial.\n\nRemember to avoid high-fat preparations, as these can worsen symptoms.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:3": 4.9103738079022365, "clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:2": 4.825457459352139, "clueweb22-en0039-65-00093:3": 4.807695909596237, "clueweb22-en0005-41-09262:15": 4.798857379087235, "clueweb22-en0044-72-05971:1": 4.709332968564811, "clueweb22-en0021-74-19197:1": 4.657335118119957, "clueweb22-en0039-15-05920:17": 4.654708889777541, "clueweb22-en0024-83-01996:17": 4.63