{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Apple cider vinegar (ACV) can worsen acid reflux for some individuals primarily due to its acidic nature. For those with an already irritated esophagus or moderate to severe acid reflux, introducing more acid can directly cause further burning and irritation.\n\nMoreover, in cases of silent reflux (LPR), stomach acid can carry the enzyme pepsin into the throat and airways. When acidic substances like ACV are consumed, they can activate this previously refluxed pepsin, increasing its damaging potential to the mucous membranes and exacerbating LPR symptoms. Additionally, if someone already has stomach issues caused by excess stomach acid or underlying gastritis, the acidity of ACV can intensify these problems.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-96-01816:1": 4.969030633264101, "clueweb22-en0002-03-17690:14": 4.835243600657418, "clueweb22-en0002-87-15707:7": 4.48775577577379, "clueweb22-en0008-10-03226:2": 4.240542693160776, "clueweb22-en0001-62-08246:7": 4.217881819096651}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0027-96-01816:1": 4.969030633264101, "clueweb22-en0002-03-17690:14": 4.835243600657418, "clueweb22-en0023-70-15463:6": 4.7938150501924035, "clueweb22-en0027-96-01816:0": 4.703175535298612, "clueweb22-en0002-03-17690:15": 4.6084003772453075, "clueweb22-en0002-87-15707:7": 4.48775577577379, "clueweb22-en0032-97-12085:3": 4.409950144920696, "clueweb22-en0002-87-15707:6": 4.308046202407215, "clueweb22-en0008-10-03226:2": 4.240542693160776, "clueweb22-en0045-72-12247:14": 4.218392097074684, "clueweb22-en0001-62-08246:7": 4.217881819096651, "clueweb22-en0027-96-01816:2": 4.161009181300701, "clueweb22-en0030-73-19245:12": 4.126526673563525, "clueweb22-en0008-10-03226:1": 4.068147187403882, "clueweb22-en0030-73-19245:11": 4.0627583660268005, "clueweb22-en0010-73-01980:11": 4.032965022242114, "clueweb22-en0000-50-