{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-2_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To address the psychological aspects of a healthier lifestyle, focus on your mindset and habits. Psychologists suggest actively editing negative self-talk; rephrase thoughts like \"I am too busy\" to \"I choose to make myself a priority\" (3, 6). Engage in stress-reduction techniques like deep breathing, meditation, or spending time in nature and sunlight, as these can significantly boost mood and reduce stress (4, 9). Social connection is also crucial; spend quality time with loved ones (4).\n\nFor managing screen time, be mindful of its impact on your psychological well-being. Excessive screen time is linked to psychological distress and can lead to social comparison and anxiety (10, 12). Set boundaries by taking breaks every 30 minutes, avoiding screens during meals, and limiting use two hours before bed (1, 15). Consider building a support system to normalize a screen-free lifestyle or replacing digital tasks with analog alternatives like a paper notebook (13).\n\nTo maintain motivation, find your personal \"why\" for making changes (2). Set small, realistic, and enjoyable goals (5, 7, 11, 19). Track your progress to stay on track (16). Engaging in activities you genuinely enjoy makes consistency easier (1, 7, 11, 17). Building habits by repeating actions in consistent contexts can make them automatic and effortless, reducing reliance on conscious motivation (20). Exercising with friends or a support system can also help you persevere (11, 17).", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0030-93-10180:12": 4.619583053267061, "clueweb22-en0024-57-18850:0": 4.549746454333034, "clueweb22-en0022-23-03836:14": 4.472114959150847, "clueweb22-en0003-83-08131:11": 4.293398909785419, "clueweb22-en0039-35-04877:11": 4.160356180517925, "clueweb22-en0022-23-03836:15": 4.146213830520642, "clueweb22-en0026-21-18156:9": 3.9926725899251005, "clueweb2