{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Garlic boosts metabolism through several mechanisms. It can raise your body temperature, which helps your body break down fats and increase the speed of your metabolism. Garlic also stimulates the release of norepinephrine, a neurotransmitter that increases your metabolic rate, leading to faster calorie burning.\n\nAdditionally, garlic helps normalize blood sugar levels, which can prevent hunger spikes and signals for fat storage. It promotes healthy blood flow and lymphatic drainage, and assists in fighting \"bad\" cholesterol. The active compound allicin in garlic is beneficial for metabolic disorders and high blood sugar. Garlic can also help restore adrenaline production, which accelerates fat breakdown, and suppress cortisol, a hormone that can contribute to weight gain. Some studies even suggest garlic can \"turn off\" genes involved in storing fat.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0005-37-20318:3": 4.962944032927783, "clueweb22-en0020-36-05174:16": 4.845526854651828, "clueweb22-en0004-67-10066:1": 4.584244703524957, "clueweb22-en0004-06-07544:2": 4.512029788187904, "clueweb22-en0032-66-14669:5": 4.226901450758779, "clueweb22-en0045-52-16501:9": 4.048372413315883, "clueweb22-en0004-06-07544:1": 4.028348378546323, "clueweb22-en0020-36-05174:17": 4.019122078457401, "clueweb22-en0013-19-04486:2": 3.9433841829102505, "clueweb22-en0041-89-08008:4": 3.891770834636677}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0005-37-20318:3": 4.962944032927783, "clueweb22-en0020-36-05174:16": 4.845526854651828, "clueweb22-en0004-67-10066:1": 4.584244703524957, "clueweb22-en0022-33-16740:14": 4.578046258877394, "clueweb22-en0004-06-07544:2": 4.512029788187904, "clueweb22-en0020-21-11393:4": 4.508481451460313, "clueweb22-en0032-66-14669:6": 4.385344031429368, "clueweb22-en0005-21-03017:2": 4.339814705415982, "clueweb22-en0005-21-03