{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Oaked Chardonnay, which often features hazelnut notes alongside rich, buttery, and creamy flavors, is produced in several key wine regions.\n\nOne of the most renowned areas is **Burgundy, France**, where Chardonnay originated. Specifically, the C\u00f4te de Beaune region in Burgundy is known for its sophisticated Chardonnays, which are typically fermented and aged in French oak barrels and can develop distinct hazelnut tones. White Burgundy wines, in general, often exhibit hazelnut aromatics.\n\nIn the **United States**, particularly in **California**, regions like Napa Valley, Sonoma County (including Russian River Valley and Sonoma Coast), and Los Carneros are well-known for producing excellent oaked Chardonnays that can carry these desired hazelnut characteristics.\n\nOther significant regions for oaked Chardonnay with hazelnut notes include **Australia**, **South Africa**, and **Puglia, Italy**. Additionally, specific oaked Chardonnays with hazelnut notes can be found in **Hawke\u2019s Bay, New Zealand**.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0022-04-12330:4": 5.0, "clueweb22-en0022-04-12330:3": 4.755306307765421, "clueweb22-en0034-95-07216:19": 4.430572753857968, "clueweb22-en0034-95-07216:18": 4.4055477595228165, "clueweb22-en0014-52-05147:7": 4.209209900183519, "clueweb22-en0038-17-14145:10": 3.7510686986738, "clueweb22-en0038-17-14145:11": 3.6832672077193545, "clueweb22-en0042-65-15241:6": 3.4448061147733875, "clueweb22-en0042-65-15241:5": 3.420505734254373}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0022-04-12330:4": 5.0, "clueweb22-en0022-04-12330:3": 4.755306307765421, "clueweb22-en0034-95-07216:19": 4.430572753857968, "clueweb22-en0034-95-07216:18": 4.4055477595228165, "clueweb22-en0014-52-05147:7": 4.209209900183519, "clueweb22-en0033-29-12915:8": 3.9750374347126556, "clueweb22-en0014-52-05147:6": 3.9581447