{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "H-taping is a highly effective method for supporting injured finger pulleys, particularly during recovery from climbing injuries. Research indicates it's more effective than other taping methods in keeping tendons snug against the bone, which helps prevent bowstringing and can even increase the crimping strength of an injured finger by about 13%.\n\nTo apply H-taping, cut a piece of rigid athletic tape (e.g., Leukoplast) 10cm long and 1.5cm wide. Then, cut it in half lengthwise from both ends, leaving a 1cm bridge in the middle. Position this bridge on the inside of your injured finger, directly on the crease of the joint above the injured pulley. Flex your finger 60 degrees at the joint you are taping. First, wrap the upper part of the tape into a ring, and then wrap the lower part into another ring below the joint. It's important to retape your finger between climbs as the tape can stretch and lose its supportive effectiveness.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 5.0, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 4.568546703385018, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:10": 4.45809857274204, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 4.312865964929476, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 4.223403586258065, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.219750039614553, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 4.028955757728725, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 3.5243562604436494}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 5.0, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 4.568546703385018, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:10": 4.45809857274204, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 4.312865964929476, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 4.223403586258065, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.219750039614553, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 4.097243033888995, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 4.028955757728725, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 3.94963403597672, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727: