{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Combining yoga and open water swimming is an excellent choice for both your recovery and overall well-being. Yoga offers significant benefits for swimmers, including optimizing mobility, improving strength, enhancing recovery, and preventing injuries. It also strengthens mental skills, body awareness, and breathing efficiency, which can help alleviate stress and improve your mind-body connection.\n\nOpen water swimming is a low-impact activity that is gentle on your joints, making it ideal for injury recovery as it strengthens muscles without strain. It also significantly increases flexibility and releases endorphins, similar to yoga, contributing to stress reduction and improved mood. Open water specifically offers unique mental challenges, can reduce chronic pain, and is known to improve sleep and boost happiness.\n\nTogether, yoga and open water swimming create a comprehensive approach to physical and mental health. Yoga's focus on flexibility and recovery complements swimming's full-body, joint-friendly workout, while both activities are powerful tools for reducing stress, improving mood, and enhancing overall well-being during your recovery.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0026-52-18893:1": 4.62943845234687, "clueweb22-en0026-52-18893:0": 4.390102727374918, "clueweb22-en0026-34-03436:0": 3.5623293272811685, "clueweb22-en0007-01-10890:6": 3.4096828456960147, "clueweb22-en0007-01-10890:5": 3.2923214268013967, "clueweb22-en0022-16-10522:10": 3.1700444381471407, "clueweb22-en0037-34-12182:6": 3.1639854018918188, "clueweb22-en0027-97-15372:0": 2.9285394878052258, "clueweb22-en0022-16-10522:11": 2.869204819553074}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0026-52-18893:1": 4.62943845234687, "clueweb22-en0026-52-18893:0": 4.390102727374918, "clueweb22-en0026-52-18893:13": 4.254642277854591, "clueweb22-en0001-05-027