{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_3", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Great, a 10 km run is a fantastic goal! It's a manageable distance for most people, and it's definitely achievable even if you're not very confident in your current fitness level.\n\nTo prepare for your 10 km run, especially as a beginner, it's ideal to allow around **eight to twelve weeks** for training. Consistency is key, so aim to run at least **three times per week**. The best approach is to build up your training gradually. Start with shorter runs (e.g., 15 minutes per session) at an easy, comfortable pace, and don't hesitate to include walking sections if needed \u2013 there's nothing wrong with that! Gradually increase your total distance by no more than 10% per week. Work towards building your long run distance up to at least 7.5 km.\n\nFor nutrition, focus on high-carbohydrate snacks before your runs and remember to stay well-hydrated. After your run, it's important to refuel; a meal like salmon with brown rice, chickpeas, and beans can be great for replenishing energy. Also, consider investing in performance running gear that wicks sweat away from your body. Incorporating strength training into your routine can also help improve your running economy and prevent injuries.\n\nRemember, simply being able to finish a 10 km race is a significant achievement, regardless of your time.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0034-83-04863:5": 4.939273694494603, "clueweb22-en0034-83-04863:0": 4.627940887769052, "clueweb22-en0007-91-03974:0": 4.612022466387349, "clueweb22-en0014-46-02248:8": 4.583251588067635, "clueweb22-en0004-91-11430:1": 4.56363607572776, "clueweb22-en0019-45-10567:5": 4.547300017609043, "clueweb22-en0019-45-10567:4": 4.4891924451643455, "clueweb22-en0008-57-08667:0": 4.386427103072993, "clueweb22-en0000-52-05962:6": 4.3849444677168234, "clueweb22-en0032-17-06111:6": 4.3488825569681575, "clueweb22-en0026-77-06464