{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Choosing the right running shoes is crucial for comfort, performance, and injury prevention. The best approach is to visit a specialty running store. Experts there can help you by assessing your foot type, gait (how your foot rolls when landing, known as pronation), and running style. They might even use a 3D scan to find your ideal fit.\n\nWhen trying on shoes, comfort is paramount \u2013 if a shoe doesn't feel right immediately, it likely won't on a run. Ensure there's about a thumb's width of space between your longest toe and the end of the shoe, and wiggle your toes to check for enough room. Don't assume your size, as it varies between brands. Consider the terrain you'll mostly run on (road, trail, etc.) and your training goals. Remember, the shoe should feel like an extension of your body. Finally, avoid wearing brand new shoes on race day; break them in for at least 100 miles beforehand.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0016-81-12613:9": 4.714520270577137, "clueweb22-en0042-93-05771:15": 4.583590645878923, "clueweb22-en0033-26-12679:2": 4.569451624941977, "clueweb22-en0031-37-17290:4": 4.537573305363472, "clueweb22-en0017-51-11925:4": 4.348112997261336, "clueweb22-en0004-94-13132:12": 4.288854759713869, "clueweb22-en0000-57-00537:11": 4.228482475510583, "clueweb22-en0026-47-01829:11": 4.181445978953805}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0000-41-18655:0": 4.8143909922752, "clueweb22-en0019-45-05584:2": 4.771516231853598, "clueweb22-en0016-81-12613:9": 4.714520270577137, "clueweb22-en0042-93-05771:15": 4.583590645878923, "clueweb22-en0033-26-12679:2": 4.569451624941977, "clueweb22-en0031-37-17290:5": 4.546112118334154, "clueweb22-en0031-37-17290:4": 4.537573305363472, "clueweb22-en0039-61-04418:1": 4.420943444510899, "clueweb22-en0005-00-00789:5": 4.4038411886695386, "clueweb22-en0033-26-12679:1": 4.36