{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For your trip to New York, here are some general tips and suggestions for places to visit:\n\n**Travel Tips:**\n*   **Getting Around:** The New York City Subway is an efficient way to travel; consider purchasing a seven-day unlimited pass if you plan on frequent use (Passage 2, 3). However, much of New York is very walkable, so pack comfortable shoes and be prepared to explore on foot (Passage 1, 19).\n*   **Payment:** While you prefer cash for small purchases, New York is a \"card-happy\" city, and it's advised not to carry large amounts of cash (Passage 15).\n*   **Planning:** For popular attractions like observation decks (Empire State Building, One World Observatory, The Edge), buying tickets online in advance can save you waiting time (Passage 6). Starting your day early can also help you avoid crowds at popular spots (Passage 18).\n*   **Best Time to Visit:** April to June, and September to October, are often recommended for pleasant weather (Passage 5, 17).\n\n**Places to Visit:**\n*   **Iconic Parks:** Spend time in Central Park, a vast and beloved urban oasis (Passage 7, 9). Bryant Park, near the Public Library, is also a great spot for events and relaxation (Passage 1, 16).\n*   **Beyond Manhattan:** While Manhattan offers famous attractions like Times Square and Broadway (Passage 9, 10), explore other boroughs. Brooklyn boasts a fantastic food scene and charming brownstones, while the Bronx is home to the New York Botanical Garden and Zoo (Passage 3, 9, 10).\n*   **Museums:** The Metropolitan Museum of Art is a world-renowned destination (Passage 11, 20). Given your preference for quiet museums, consider visiting The Cloisters, a tranquil branch of the Met focusing on medieval art and architecture (Passage 13).\n*   **Views:** For breathtaking cityscapes, visit observation decks like The Edge Hudson Yards or One World Observatory (Passage 6).\n*   **Food:** Don't miss out on the city's diverse culinary scene, from street food stands to delicious doughnuts (Passage 7, 12, 14).", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:19": 4.775403251061139, "clueweb22-en0036-97-04646:0": 4.757292785370382, "clueweb22-en0036-97-04646:1": 4.731707870535703, "clueweb22-en0017-05-13815:2": 4.547937243920858, "clueweb22-en0017-05-13815:12": 4.452360133149234, "clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:8": 4.43735307866657, "clueweb22-en0006-35-04334:1": 4.39999004229159, "clueweb22-en0043-93-03149:2": 4.3593595645788135, "clueweb22-en0020-88-00965:2": 4.358989738926743, "clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:21": 4.35486336499383, "clueweb22-en0011-88-06933:3": 4.350938740500513, "clueweb22-en0002-97-05324:6": 4.348293762103778, "clueweb22-en0022-50-07286:11": 4.348055408986789, "clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:18": 4.297338490309561, "clueweb22-en0017-05-13815:1": 4.288428230542204, "clueweb22-en0029-37-01132:6": 4.270931208938309, "clueweb22-en0014-32-01646:9": 4.259898028005201, "clueweb22-en0016-37-14198:8": 4.253931093637059}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:19": 4.775403251061139, "clueweb22-en0036-97-04646:0": 4.757292785370382, "clueweb22-en0036-97-04646:1": 4.731707870535703, "clueweb22-en0007-91-02351:9": 4.599767447161824, "clueweb22-en0017-05-13815:2": 4.547937243920858, "clueweb22-en0017-05-13815:12": 4.452360133149234, "clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:8": 4.43735307866657, "clueweb22-en0036-98-16848:9": 4.418743929598139, "clueweb22-en0006-35-04334:1": 4.39999004229159, "clueweb22-en0043-93-03149:2": 4.3593595645788135, "clueweb22-en0020-88-00965:2": 4.358989738926743, "clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:21": 4.35486336499383, "clueweb22-en0011-88-06933:3": 4.350938740500513, "clueweb22-en0002-97-05324:6": 4.348293762103778, "clueweb22-en0022-50-07286:11": 4.348055408986789, "clueweb22-en0029-07-09423:18": 4.297338490309561, "clueweb22-en0017-05-13815:1": 4.288428230542204, "clueweb22-en0029-3