{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For healthier, low-carb, and nutrient-rich lunch alternatives to white rice, you have several excellent options:\n\n*   **Cauliflower Rice:** This is a very popular low-carb substitute, offering a similar texture to white rice. It's low in calories and packed with fiber, Vitamin C, Vitamin K, and folate. You can easily make it yourself or buy it pre-riced.\n*   **Shirataki Rice:** Also known as \"miracle rice,\" it's made from the konjac plant and is extremely low in carbs (often 1 gram net carb or less per serving) and calories, while being a good source of fiber and iron.\n*   **Broccoli Rice:** Similar to cauliflower rice, it's a low-carb option rich in fiber, plant protein, and iron.\n*   **Rutabaga Rice:** This root vegetable alternative is low in net carbs (around 7.9 grams per cup) and provides Vitamin C, potassium, and manganese.\n\nBeyond these rice-like substitutes, consider incorporating other low-carb, high-nutrient foods into your lunch:\n\n*   **Chickpeas:** These are high in fiber and protein, making them a filling and nutritious low-carb side dish or meal component.\n*   **Protein-focused meals:** You can create low-carb Bento box lunches featuring an egg and other proteins. Rolling up sliced deli meat with thin vegetables and cheese is another simple, low-carb option.\n*   **Fresh Salads:** Opt for a fresh salad with chicken or explore keto salad recipes for a nutrient-dense, low-carb meal.\n\nThese alternatives will help you maintain a low-carb diet while boosting your nutrient and protein intake.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0043-00-14527:4": 4.744334504317431, "clueweb22-en0017-78-15809:1": 4.540615372202484, "clueweb22-en0011-92-17473:6": 4.362661938865608, "clueweb22-en0007-64-04958:26": 4.213802635237327, "clueweb22-en0003-12-08571:2": 4.098090131199314, "clueweb22-en0021-52-06526:2": 4.0915889672429