{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly! Beyond the rice alternatives, there are many other low-carb and high-nutrient options for your lunch.\n\nYou can create various **wraps** using large lettuce leaves (like romaine or iceberg) as a substitute for bread or tortillas. Fill them with roasted turkey, grilled chicken, deli meats, cheese, and vegetables, or even make spicy taco wraps.\n\nFor **noodle or pasta alternatives**, consider spiralized zucchini (zoodles) for dishes like Pad Thai, or spaghetti squash as a base for Bolognese or lasagna. Cauliflower rice also works wonderfully for fried rice dishes.\n\n**Salads** are a fantastic choice. Opt for protein-rich options like tuna salad, chicken salad, egg salad, or steak salad, served on a bed of mixed greens. You can also explore various vegetable-heavy salads with ingredients like halloumi cheese, avocado, or shrimp ceviche.\n\nOther high-protein, low-carb ideas include **bunless burgers**, grilled chicken or salmon, Tamagoyaki (a Japanese omelet), mini quiches, or meat-based dishes like meatballs and mini meatloaf. You can also assemble **\"lunch bowls\"** with a base of lean protein (chicken, salmon), healthy fats (avocado), and plenty of non-starchy vegetables like broccoli or bell peppers.\n\nThese options offer a great way to boost your nutrient intake while keeping carbs low.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0038-04-16873:16": 4.640351321133318, "clueweb22-en0043-00-14527:5": 4.599910831491386, "clueweb22-en0003-79-04263:2": 4.584786103570619, "clueweb22-en0038-73-08261:5": 4.480238864776213, "clueweb22-en0011-92-17473:6": 4.461445671300932, "clueweb22-en0038-73-08261:6": 4.4204597236767516, "clueweb22-en0007-71-04630:15": 4.380438637938232, "clueweb22-en0039-79-15384:7": 4.375101586665348, "clueweb22-en0046-52-04250:5": 4.358266503027852, "clueweb22-en0018-67-19152:5": 4.349926635067047, "clueweb2