{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Breastfeeding can indeed be a subject of controversy and presents various challenges. One significant area of debate revolves around public breastfeeding, with some people finding it uncomfortable or considering it public indecency due to the exposure of the mother's body.\n\nBeyond public perception, controversies also arise from the strong advocacy for \"breast is best,\" which can lead to a backlash. Some mothers who are unable to breastfeed, or choose not to, report feeling shamed, guilty, or even \"persecuted.\" It's recognized that not all women produce enough milk, and factors like returning to work can make sustained breastfeeding very difficult.\n\nFrom a personal standpoint, breastfeeding can have negative aspects. It demands significant energy, can cause fatigue, nausea, breast tenderness, nipple soreness, and irritability, especially if you are pregnant. Mothers also need to be mindful of their diet and medications, as these can pass to the baby. While generally safe, if you are pregnant, your doctor might advise against continued breastfeeding if you have a high-risk pregnancy, are carrying multiples, experience uterine pain or bleeding, or are advised to avoid sex. Your milk supply may also decrease and change in taste during pregnancy.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0034-27-16750:1": 4.4686112766852615, "clueweb22-en0017-54-18029:7": 4.236334351828964, "clueweb22-en0012-14-02860:1": 4.227987459827232, "clueweb22-en0037-81-01263:5": 4.139692554458495, "clueweb22-en0005-46-00778:1": 4.082582189692043, "clueweb22-en0004-74-03935:10": 4.080667672064411, "clueweb22-en0032-87-04765:4": 4.049610406757546, "clueweb22-en0012-32-04859:4": 4.020892774196572, "clueweb22-en0034-27-16750:6": 4.005478594763332, "clueweb22-en0011-87-07940:2": 3.9709548153490175, "clueweb22-en0017-54-18029:8": 3.898147986014364, "clueweb22-en0