{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Jam can certainly be part of a healthy diet during pregnancy! When made with fully ripened fruits, jam can be a concentrated source of nutrition, offering heart-healthy, cancer-fighting antioxidants. Some sources suggest that the nutrients in fruit jam, particularly folate, can help reduce the risk of neural tube defects like spina bifida during fetal development. For example, strawberry jam is noted for being beneficial in pregnancy and helping to regulate blood pressure. The pectin commonly used as a gelling agent in jams is also generally considered safe for consumption in small amounts during pregnancy.\n\nHowever, as with many foods, moderation is key, especially since jams often contain added sugars. While a sample daily menu for pregnant women can include a small amount of jam, it's important to be mindful of your overall sugar intake. If you are managing gestational diabetes or have been advised to limit sweeteners, it's recommended to avoid jam and honey, or choose varieties with no added sugar. As mentioned before, the goal is to eat a wide range of foods, so enjoy your jam but also mix it up with other nutritious options!", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-61-18698:10": 4.668132111496305, "clueweb22-en0031-32-15160:5": 4.341235983061228, "clueweb22-en0023-61-18698:9": 4.169748756213587, "clueweb22-en0031-32-15160:4": 4.130880125926442, "clueweb22-en0008-26-06180:3": 3.9345403045342646, "clueweb22-en0024-03-03906:18": 3.9150052752905062, "clueweb22-en0009-11-11998:4": 3.6787158823186883, "clueweb22-en0004-19-10146:12": 3.5388542423022464, "clueweb22-en0008-88-00414:7": 3.5048488354676652, "clueweb22-en0024-03-03906:17": 3.504562745224039}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0023-61-18698:10": 4.668132111496305, "clueweb22-en0004-76-13303:1": 4.603635394385249, "clueweb22-en0004-76-13303:2": 4.499