{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Microneedling, also known as percutaneous collagen induction therapy, works by creating tiny, controlled micro-injuries in the skin using fine needles. These microscopic punctures are not large enough to cause scarring; instead, they trigger your body's natural wound-healing process.\n\nWhen the skin detects these micro-injuries, it responds by stimulating the production of new collagen and elastin. Collagen is the main support structure of the skin, and elastin provides elasticity. As we age, the production of these proteins slows down, leading to issues like fine lines, wrinkles, and sagging. By boosting their synthesis, microneedling helps to repair damaged cells, improve skin texture and tone, reduce the appearance of scars, dark spots, and enlarged pores, and make the skin firmer and smoother. This process essentially remodels the skin, leading to a more youthful and radiant complexion.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0025-75-16875:1": 4.950796752819318, "clueweb22-en0038-11-18082:2": 4.689764431447674, "clueweb22-en0042-13-06743:2": 4.649041212708816, "clueweb22-en0040-85-11815:5": 4.5982399799563245, "clueweb22-en0004-83-01928:2": 4.444192750914579, "clueweb22-en0013-78-16369:1": 4.315418209378072, "clueweb22-en0037-79-06507:1": 4.299363312195725}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0025-75-16875:1": 4.950796752819318, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:3": 4.836773398393367, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:2": 4.727374606286657, "clueweb22-en0006-25-14668:4": 4.722907850676026, "clueweb22-en0038-11-18082:2": 4.689764431447674, "clueweb22-en0017-43-06405:12": 4.682856454459272, "clueweb22-en0042-13-06743:2": 4.649041212708816, "clueweb22-en0003-80-18647:2": 4.637566436752584, "clueweb22-en0030-73-16433:1": 4.62742117821912, "clueweb22-en0040-85-11815:5": 4.5982399799563245, "clueweb22-en0006-25-14668:3": 4.5770678