{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You should avoid using your face wash with salicylic acid immediately after microneedling. Products containing salicylic acid, glycolic acid, or other exfoliating acids (AHAs/BHAs) should not be used as they can irritate or harm your skin after the treatment. It's recommended to wait at least three days, and ideally a week, before reintroducing such products.\n\nFor your oily skin, it's best to temporarily switch to gentle, hydrating, and non-irritating products. Your skin's barrier is more vulnerable post-treatment, so focus on mild cleansers and moisturizers, and ingredients like hyaluronic acid, peptides, and ceramides, which aid in healing and hydration.\n\nRegarding products for your oily scalp and hair, it is advised to refrain from your regular hair care routines immediately after microneedling. While specific products for oily hair aren't detailed, the general advice is to be gentle and minimalistic. Be cautious to prevent any harsh hair products from coming into contact with your treated facial skin, and avoid direct high heat from blow dryers.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:11": 4.72661706888649, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:12": 4.591369632155297, "clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:7": 4.493337187739938, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": 4.3140273408721725, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:2": 4.130884076584278, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:1": 4.084600816595338, "clueweb22-en0001-02-00582:10": 3.7721883767736486, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:9": 3.7507135199503043, "clueweb22-en0030-73-16433:6": 3.705430851065179, "clueweb22-en0015-70-17166:2": 3.5957097154288595, "clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:6": 3.565630170024348, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:4": 3.521341928677585}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:11": 4.72661706888649, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:12": 4.591369632155297, "clueweb22-en0009-