{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage your oily scalp while addressing the effects of frequent heat styling, look for shampoos that contain a balance of clarifying and nourishing ingredients.\n\nFor oil control, seek out ingredients like salicylic acid, tea tree oil, eucalyptus oil, peppermint oil, and citrus extracts. Natural plant extracts such as ginseng, chamomile, green tea, echinacea, sage, and rosemary can also help cleanse and balance the scalp. Clarifying shampoos can be beneficial for deep cleansing, but use them in moderation.\n\nGiven your frequent heat styling, it's crucial to also look for ingredients that moisturize and protect your hair without adding weight. Consider shampoos with argan oil, coconut oil, shea butter, biotin, baobab, hyaluronic acid, keratin, or glycerine, which help hydrate and strengthen the hair cuticle.\n\nCrucially, avoid harsh chemicals like Sodium Lauryl Sulfate (SLS), Sodium Laureth Sulfate (SLES), parabens, and alcohol, as these can strip natural oils, irritate your scalp, and exacerbate dryness from heat styling. Opt for sulfate-free formulations to maintain scalp health and hair moisture. Additionally, always use a high-quality heat protectant containing ingredients like argan oil, coconut oil, or keratin when styling.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-83-04895:7": 4.824057880812964, "clueweb22-en0006-71-15684:13": 4.795685254524624, "clueweb22-en0009-83-04895:8": 4.60639839200073, "clueweb22-en0004-58-08945:6": 4.552963155972698, "clueweb22-en0009-83-04895:6": 4.522045374393086, "clueweb22-en0001-52-06865:20": 4.398096519124984, "clueweb22-en0037-41-10440:5": 4.350724990704988, "clueweb22-en0039-71-11631:17": 4.316032469018762, "clueweb22-en0044-18-15248:16": 4.310056250932144, "clueweb22-en0043-89-01750:4": 4.23587314608942, "clueweb22-en0007-83-07134:12": 4.20907380906803, "clueweb22-en0001-52-06865:21":