{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Baking bread at home is a rewarding experience, and with your basic baking experience, you're in a great position to start! Many resources cater to home bakers of all levels, from complete beginners to those looking to refine their skills.\n\nFor suitable guidance and recipes, you could explore:\n*   **No-Knead Bread:** This is often recommended for beginners and those with some experience, as it requires minimal hands-on work. Cookbooks like \"My Bread\" by Jim Lahey are famous for this technique (Passages 3, 8, 12).\n*   **Cookbooks:** Several excellent books are designed for home bakers. \"Josey Baker Bread\" is recommended for beginners interested in sourdough, progressing in difficulty, while \"Dough \u2013 Richard Bertinet\" covers basic techniques and recipes (Passages 3, 7, 8, 11).\n*   **Online Resources:** Websites like Breadtopia offer instructional videos, recipes, and tips for getting started with artisan bread (Passage 20). You can also find many beginner-friendly recipes, such as those for basic sandwich bread (Passage 10).\n*   **Workshops:** If you prefer hands-on learning, some bakeries offer workshops for both beginners and more experienced home bakers (Passage 15).\n\nBaking your own bread allows you to control ingredients, avoid additives, and customize flavors, leading to healthier and more delicious results (Passages 1, 4, 6, 14). Don't be discouraged if your first loaf isn't perfect; persistence is key (Passages 13, 16).", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0034-33-08941:3": 4.353781748411037, "clueweb22-en0009-68-10412:1": 4.1879989135483235, "clueweb22-en0026-16-06298:2": 4.153888196861597, "clueweb22-en0000-35-08966:4": 4.098347548587158, "clueweb22-en0022-60-14475:8": 4.065609862252393, "clueweb22-en0006-74-13319:2": 4.058230892713843, "clueweb22-en0009-68-10412:0": 3.97523107364305, "clueweb22-en0037-0