{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To bake bread at home in an oven, beyond basic kitchen tools, several items can significantly improve your results and experience.\n\nEssential items include a **large mixing bowl** (a round stainless steel one is often recommended) and a **plastic scraper** for handling dough.\n\nFor professional-quality bread and better crust, a **Dutch oven** is highly recommended as it traps steam, which is crucial for crust development. Alternatively, you can use a **baking stone** or **oven tiles** to replicate the high heat of bakery ovens, along with a cast iron skillet to create steam.\n\nFor precision, a **kitchen scale** is invaluable as volume measurements can be inaccurate. A **bread thermometer** helps ensure your bread reaches the correct internal temperature for safety and doneness. A **scoring lame** allows you to make controlled cuts on the dough surface.\n\nOther useful tools include a **cooling rack** for proper cooling and additional **dough and bowl scrapers**. If you prefer not to knead by hand, a **stand mixer** or **dough mixer** can be a great investment, though not essential for starting out.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0030-47-17290:2": 4.893958211236173, "clueweb22-en0016-38-16516:1": 4.767141629608135, "clueweb22-en0000-03-01428:1": 4.715167553589548, "clueweb22-en0039-39-06219:8": 4.670900837061207, "clueweb22-en0012-22-15186:2": 4.500558102626549, "clueweb22-en0015-38-19100:8": 4.478780696896701}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0030-47-17290:2": 4.893958211236173, "clueweb22-en0016-38-16516:1": 4.767141629608135, "clueweb22-en0000-03-01428:1": 4.715167553589548, "clueweb22-en0039-39-06219:8": 4.670900837061207, "clueweb22-en0002-32-10950:2": 4.658949338534488, "clueweb22-en0019-84-10705:4": 4.509490122003044, "clueweb22-en0012-22-15186:2": 4.500558102626549, "clueweb22-en0018-61-14372