{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Managing ADHD effectively in your office job, especially with a sedentary lifestyle, involves specific strategies to address common symptoms like hyperactivity, distractibility, and memory issues.\n\nTo counter the sedentary nature of your work and manage hyperactivity, take frequent intermittent breaks to move around, such as walking to the mailroom or water fountain. Consider using your lunch hour for exercise instead of going out. Taking notes during meetings can also help prevent restlessness.\n\nFor distractibility, a common challenge in an office environment, try requesting a private office or quiet cubicle, or work during off-peak hours. Using white noise or noise-cancelling headphones can help drown out office sounds. To manage internal distractions like daydreaming, jot down ideas in a notebook to avoid interrupting your current task, and use to-do lists to stay focused. Maintaining an organized, clutter-free workspace can also minimize distractions.\n\nTo improve memory, utilize tools like tape recorders or copious notes for meetings, create checklists for complex tasks, and use computer reminders for deadlines. If impulsivity is a challenge, practice self-talk, seek regular constructive feedback, and develop routines for coping with frustrating situations. Additionally, consider working with a psychologist, life coach, or career counselor for personalized strategies and support.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:4": 4.741115986285877, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:5": 4.569855045415925, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:1": 4.542255589975883, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:10": 4.448310546767663, "clueweb22-en0017-60-15663:1": 4.3855152805502895, "clueweb22-en0038-52-05284:13": 4.238801592819627, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:0": 4.20173563177361, "clueweb22-en0040-18-11535:11": 4.143607494226295, "clueweb22-en0019-85-0