{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Feeling overwhelmed by the number of tasks at work is a common challenge for adults with ADHD. Here are some strategies that can help you manage this:\n\nFirst, tackle large or complex projects by breaking them down into smaller, more manageable pieces. This makes them feel less daunting and easier to start. You can even set a deadline for each small step and reward yourself upon completion \u2013 these rewards don't need to be grand, just something you enjoy.\n\nTo manage your overall workload, prioritize your tasks. Instead of a long, overwhelming to-do list, try scheduling one or two essential tasks for specific times. This can make them feel more attainable. It's also crucial to avoid over-scheduling yourself; practice saying \"no\" to new projects if you're already feeling stretched. Focus on completing one task before starting another.\n\nConsider using tools like a task manager or calendar to keep track of your responsibilities and deadlines. If possible, you might also find it helpful to work with a co-worker or supervisor to set deadlines or delegate certain tasks, providing an extra layer of accountability and support.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:11": 4.844372728883648, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:7": 4.754734323851888, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:8": 4.727983689863948, "clueweb22-en0029-09-07368:2": 4.674229171553567, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 4.663570754134764, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:11": 4.630749649031884, "clueweb22-en0002-41-06891:5": 4.597396995242962, "clueweb22-en0001-03-06965:6": 4.511424162612893, "clueweb22-en0023-70-01917:23": 4.476831971946372, "clueweb22-en0002-41-06891:4": 4.4570624751541414, "clueweb22-en0022-96-02784:5": 4.400516316514268, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:9": 4.386178865347696, "clueweb22-en0017-60-15663:5": 4.370639267911476, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:11": 4.355