{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It's very common for individuals with ADHD to struggle with task completion and jumping between different responsibilities without finishing them. This can certainly feel overwhelming and unproductive.\n\nA highly effective strategy to combat this is to focus on completing one task at a time. Avoid starting a new task until your current one is fully done. This helps you concentrate your attention and prevents the feeling of being scattered.\n\nTo make this easier, especially with larger projects, continue to break them down into smaller, more manageable steps, as we discussed. This way, each \"one task\" you focus on is achievable, reducing the likelihood of feeling overwhelmed and needing to switch. You might also find it helpful to use tools like timers (e.g., the Pomodoro Technique) to dedicate specific blocks of time to a single task, or to schedule your tasks rather than just having a general to-do list. This structured approach can significantly improve your focus and help you see tasks through to completion.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0035-93-06191:0": 4.352520589347786, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:3": 4.285594403619881, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 4.247139754854972, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:0": 4.1382763202455815, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:9": 4.126676549909767, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:2": 4.068524226479667, "clueweb22-en0029-09-07368:1": 3.980880361273218}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:2": 4.517373741733854, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:1": 4.5039537161390575, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:11": 4.438429144121767, "clueweb22-en0035-93-06191:0": 4.352520589347786, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:3": 4.285594403619881, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 4.247139754854972, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:8": 4.242047682943089, "clueweb22-en0019-85-03855:11": 4.20923856494779, "clueweb22-en