{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage transitions before and after meetings and help reset your focus, several strategies can be very effective:\n\n**Before a meeting:**\n*   **Create a mental buffer:** Take a 60-second time-out to reground yourself, or a minute of timed silence to clear your head and mentally prepare.\n*   **Meditate or breathe:** Use a short meditation or a few deep breaths to find focus before the meeting begins.\n*   **Set intentions:** Remind yourself why you're there and what you aim to accomplish, which can help you mentally transition into the meeting.\n\n**After a meeting:**\n*   **Take micro-breaks:** Immediately after a meeting, step away from your desk, shake out your body, stretch, or take a few deep breaths. This physical shift helps reset your mental energy.\n*   **Implement a \"psychological buffer zone\":** Dedicate a quick two-minute mental reset before moving to your next task. Getting out of your chair and changing your physical location, even briefly, can be very effective.\n*   **Reboot with meditation:** A short meditation can help you regain energy and focus once the meeting has ended.\n*   **Schedule buffers:** When possible, encourage shorter meetings (e.g., 25 or 50 minutes instead of an hour) to naturally build in these crucial transition times.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-69-08765:9": 4.955067998386365, "clueweb22-en0025-36-11059:6": 4.249552116361859, "clueweb22-en0002-56-12919:6": 4.1419099819224074, "clueweb22-en0023-66-19436:5": 4.139428512059906, "clueweb22-en0041-78-03980:4": 4.101065083587933, "clueweb22-en0017-46-05051:7": 4.081687696497749, "clueweb22-en0006-00-08364:14": 4.021304888784286, "clueweb22-en0022-70-00626:6": 4.017880920608267, "clueweb22-en0021-80-10230:3": 4.008315773202881}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0023-69-08765:9": 4.955067998386365, "clueweb22-