{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-base-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Here are the steps to use your chain breaker tool to open your bike chain:\n\n1.  **Understand the Chain Parts**: Your bike chain is made of outer plates, inner plates, rollers, and pins. The chain tool works by pushing one of these pins out to disconnect a link.\n2.  **Position the Chain Tool**: Your chain tool has two small prongs next to a metal pin. Find a link on your chain where you want to break it. Slide this link in between the two prongs of the tool so it's securely in place, with the prongs fitting into the gaps on either side of the link.\n3.  **Align the Driving Pin**: Make sure the chain tool's driving pin (the small metal pin that moves) is perfectly lined up with the center of one of the chain's rivets (the small circular part holding the link together). You may need to unscrew the tool's handle a bit to retract the driving pin before you can place the tool on the chain.\n4.  **Push the Pin Out**: Once aligned, slowly turn the handle of the chain tool clockwise. This will push the driving pin into the chain's rivet. Keep turning the handle firmly and steadily. You'll feel resistance as the pin starts to move.\n5.  **Break the Chain**: Continue pushing the rivet out until it's almost completely out of the link, but still slightly protruding from the other side. Then, turn the handle counterclockwise to retract the driving pin. Now, carefully wiggle the link with your fingers until it separates. Be gentle to avoid deforming the link.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 4.442041993239501, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:3": 4.2862691107083535, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:3": 4.026778218775788, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:6": 3.902694434670321}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 4.442041993239501, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:8": 4.416672959769817, "clueweb22-en0020-78-158